From: Steam-Link-PS5
Subject: window: resync instead of freezing when the host races beyond the window

IHS_SessionPacketsWindowAdd ignored any packet whose id was more than a whole
window (2048 packets) ahead of the tail. On a Wi-Fi link a single loss burst
that large freezes the tail there: every subsequent packet is also beyond the
window and dropped, the window never fills so the overflow reset never fires,
and the data channel is wedged for the rest of the session - the picture
freezes while new video keeps arriving with ever-higher ids (measured on a PS5:
36 video frames submitted, then zero while the host sent ids climbing past
18000 at 550 packets/s). Return false in that case so the caller's overflow
handler resets the window, re-adds this packet as the new tail, and signals
DataLost to pull a keyframe - the same forward resync a jitter buffer does.

diff -ru a/src/session/window.c b/src/session/window.c
--- a/src/session/window.c	2026-10-08 20:23:17.781259177 -0700
+++ b/src/session/window.c	2026-10-08 20:23:17.831051168 -0700
@@ -95,9 +95,18 @@
     if (tailOffset < 0 && -tailOffset > IHS_SessionPacketsWindowSize(window)) {
         return true;
     }
-    /* Not sure why but the offset is significantly larger than window capacity. Ignore it reset */
+    /*
+     * The host is more than a whole window ahead of us: a loss burst dropped so
+     * many packets that the one that would advance the tail never came. The
+     * original code ignored the packet, but that freezes the tail forever -
+     * every later packet is now also beyond the window and dropped, so the
+     * channel never recovers (a frozen picture while audio keeps going, no
+     * overflow logged because Add keeps "succeeding"). Treat it like an
+     * overflow so the caller resets the window, resyncs to this packet, and
+     * asks the host for a keyframe.
+     */
     if (tailOffset > window->capacity) {
-        return true;
+        return false;
     }
     /* Large offset means overflow, abort processing and hangup */
     if (tailOffset > (int) IHS_SessionPacketsWindowAvailable(window)) {
